<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  CHILL_RIME_TERRACES_1 — the Chill seabed's own two floor terrains.
  Replaces the shared RM_SeaFloorGround (RM_SeaFloorGround.xml, sediment)
  for the Chill's pocket map ONLY — every other sea-dive floor (Scald, Grey
  Sea, Twilight Sea) is untouched; see GenStep_SeaFloorTerrain.cs's own
  header for the branch.

  Owner, typed verbatim, 2026-09-27: the floor beneath is "solid ice
  sparkling with strange interaction with hydrocarbon life." At the Chill's
  -110C ambient (CHILL_THERMAL_ENGINE_1), water ice is harder than most
  rock, so the BASE terrain (RM_ChillIceBedrock) is bedrock-hard, not a
  soft/slow surface — pathCost matches the sibling RM_SeaFloorGround's own
  6 (a flat, easy floor), not a punishing one.

  On top of it: rime terraces (RM_ChillRimeTerrace), the one terrain
  character adopted at the same sitting — "the Krellik shed their
  hydrocarbon frost plates nightly and have for ten thousand years, so
  whole districts of the floor are stepped pale dunes of shed rime. Soft
  going (movement penalty), glittering loose; snowdrifts made of molted
  armor." Painted as coherent districts by GenStep_ChillRimeTerraces.cs,
  never scattered per-tile.

  PATHCOST REASONING (rime terrace, 40): compared against this codebase's
  and vanilla's own terrain family —
    RM_SeaFloorGround (sediment, this mod's own baseline flat floor): 6
    SoilRich / Ice (vanilla, ordinary walkable ground): 2 / 14
    Marsh (vanilla, a real "wade through it" tax): 30
    RM_DeepSand (this session, DEEP_SAND_WALKABLE_TERRAIN_1, "sinks...
      slowly and completely," walkable but genuinely punishing): 300
  Rime terrace is loose drift snow you sink an inch into with every step —
  worse than Marsh's mud-wade, but a small fraction of Deep Sand's
  sinking-and-fighting (these are stepped dunes of shed armor plate, not a
  medium that swallows you). 40 reads as a real, felt slowdown — about 1.3x
  Marsh — while staying nowhere near Deep Sand's territory, matching the
  item's own instruction ("gentler than 300... a real but not punishing
  slowdown").

  ART — PLACEHOLDER, same posture as every other sea-dive floor terrain
  this session (RM_SeaFloorGround/Sand, RM_DeepSand/SoftSand): checked
  infrastructure/artpipe/{done,pending}/registry.jsonl first — no existing
  ice-bedrock or rime-terrace terrain art (MEASURED 2026-09-28, no hit on
  any spelling). RM_ChillIceBedrock reuses vanilla's own literal
  Terrain/Surfaces/Ice (an honest placeholder — it IS ice). RM_ChillRimeTerrace
  reuses vanilla Terrain/Surfaces/Gravel for its mottled, non-smooth read —
  deliberately NOT the same texture as the base so the district reads as a
  visually distinct feature per the item's own deliverable 2. Real "pale
  stepped drifts of shed frost plate" art is owed alongside it, not this
  pass's to generate.

  Neither def overrides filthAcceptanceMask — both inherit
  NaturalTerrainBase's [Unnatural] mask unchanged, so
  RM_MapComponent_ChillFootprints (CHILL_THERMAL_FOOTPRINTS_1) keeps
  depositing RM_Filth_ChillFrostGlaze on both the base ice and the rime
  terraces with no patch needed — same reasoning that file's own header
  already worked out for RM_SeaFloorGround.
-->
<Defs>

  <TerrainDef ParentName="NaturalTerrainBase">
    <defName>RM_ChillIceBedrock</defName>
    <label>ice bedrock</label>
    <description>Water ice, and at these temperatures water ice is harder than most rock. The floor of the Chill is a single sheet of it, sparkling faintly under the aurora, veined here and there with something that reacts to the frozen hydrocarbon above it in ways nobody down here has explained yet.</description>
    <texturePath>Terrain/Surfaces/Ice</texturePath>
    <!-- PLACEHOLDER ART — see header. -->
    <isPaintable>false</isPaintable>
    <edgeType>FadeRough</edgeType>
    <renderPrecedence>350</renderPrecedence>
    <pathCost>6</pathCost>
    <!-- Matches sibling RM_SeaFloorGround exactly — bedrock, not a soft
         surface; see header for the comparison table. -->
    <statBases>
      <Beauty>1</Beauty>
      <BeautyOutdoors>1</BeautyOutdoors>
      <Cleanliness>1</Cleanliness>
    </statBases>
    <affordances>
      <li>Light</li>
      <li>Medium</li>
      <li>Heavy</li>
    </affordances>
    <fertility>0</fertility>
    <takeFootprints>true</takeFootprints>
    <tags>
      <li>RM_ChillIceBedrock</li>
    </tags>
  </TerrainDef>

  <TerrainDef ParentName="NaturalTerrainBase">
    <defName>RM_ChillRimeTerrace</defName>
    <label>rime terrace</label>
    <description>A stepped dune of shed hydrocarbon frost, glittering and loose underfoot -- the Krellik have been molting their plates here every night for ten thousand years, and the drift is deep enough now to slow a walking stride. It is snow made of shed armor.</description>
    <texturePath>Terrain/Surfaces/Gravel</texturePath>
    <!-- PLACEHOLDER ART — see header. -->
    <isPaintable>false</isPaintable>
    <edgeType>FadeRough</edgeType>
    <renderPrecedence>353</renderPrecedence>
    <pathCost>40</pathCost>
    <!-- See header for the full comparison table this is tuned against. -->
    <statBases>
      <Beauty>2</Beauty>
      <BeautyOutdoors>2</BeautyOutdoors>
      <Cleanliness>0</Cleanliness>
    </statBases>
    <affordances>
      <li>Light</li>
      <li>Medium</li>
      <li>Heavy</li>
    </affordances>
    <fertility>0</fertility>
    <takeFootprints>true</takeFootprints>
    <tags>
      <li>RM_ChillRimeTerrace</li>
    </tags>
  </TerrainDef>

</Defs>
